  "block_build_note": "this lane's own in-memory build, 2 threads, from logs/gbm-class.log and logs/maybe-reprice.log",
  "what_a_new_FOLD_month_actually_needs": "base.load() needs the v10 panel, the stack-5 OOF vector and the v12 vectors on the month.  None exists for a non-fold month, so a new fold month costs an OUT-OF-FOLD REFIT of the base head, which is another lane's compute and dwarfs the block build.",
  "what_a_new_FITTING_month_needs": "nothing but the block: arms fit on r12 of the ROTATION folds, so a month can enter as fitting data only if it carries p12 too.  A month with no base prediction can still widen the matcher's prefix frame and the neighbour families, which need no label and no head."
 },
